# Build context for apps/api/Dockerfile.
#
# Owned by whoever does deployment, like the Dockerfile beside it — see the team
# plan, §1. Chamodh: if something you need is missing from the image, ask rather
# than editing this.
#
# Without this file the build context was 253 MB, almost all of it .venv — a
# Windows/Linux-mismatched virtualenv that the image would never use anyway.
# Docker sends the whole context to the daemon before the first instruction
# runs, so this is pure waiting.

# Local virtualenvs. The image installs its own with pip.
.venv
venv
env

# Python bytecode and tool caches.
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.import_linter_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# Secrets and local settings. The image gets its configuration from the
# environment at run time — never from a file baked into a layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Tests are run by CI, not inside the image.
tests

# Scratch space for clones. Never part of an image.
var
/var/tmp

# Editor and VCS.
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea

# Itself.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

.DS_Store

# vendor/ — no longer copied into the image. The CK jar is fetched and checksummed
# by the Dockerfile itself (J4.1), so anything left in here is a local artefact.
# Without this line a hand-downloaded ck.jar adds 16 MB to every build context,
# which is the exact problem this file was created to solve (log Entry 2).
vendor/
